Warforged are sentient constructs created by [[House Cannith]] as soldiers for the [[Last War]]. The Treaty of Thronehold granted them legal personhood and freedom from servitude in 996 YK, but social integration remains deeply contested.

!! Construction
Warforged are built from a magical composite of wood, stone, and metal, animated by a bound creation spark. They do not need food, water, or sleep, though they can rest to recover. They feel pain and emotion, develop distinct personalities through experience, and can be permanently killed — they are not replaceable units.

[[House Cannith]] creation forges produced warforged in quantity during the Last War. Most were located in [[Cyre]]; the Day of Mourning destroyed nearly all of them. House Cannith's ability to create new warforged is now severely limited.

!! Post-War Status
The Treaty of Thronehold legally freed warforged but provided no material support for integration. They have no recognized homeland, no guaranteed legal protections beyond the treaty text, and face prejudice from organic populations who associate them with wartime trauma.

